        {
          "insert": "A Section's Name Is Its Tag"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-block-vocabulary-a-sectionnode-carries-13": {
      "id": "b-40-block-vocabulary-a-sectionnode-carries-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A "
        },
        {
          "insert": "SectionNode",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries an optional "
        },
        {
          "insert": "title",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " property, and the XML renderer\nnever reads it: the open tag is composed from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tag",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attrs",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " only (see\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Rendering Model",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/30-rendering-model"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). A \"title\" field on a\nsection would therefore be dead input, it would change the document and its\ncontent hash while changing nothing about the rendered prompt. The editor has\nno such field. A section's name is its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tag",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", edited in place on the open-tag\nrow, and everything else that appears in the open tag is an entry in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attrs",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", what the inspector calls the section's fields."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-block-vocabulary-tag-sanitization-keeps-a-14": {
      "id": "b-40-block-vocabulary-tag-sanitization-keeps-a-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Tag sanitization keeps a typed tag renderable: whitespace becomes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "_",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and the\ncharacters that would break the tag out of its own brackets are dropped.\nAnything else is left exactly as typed, so an invalid name still reaches\nvalidation, which reports it and blocks the save, rather than being silently\nrewritten under the caret. Attribute keys get the parallel treatment."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
